# Feature Module Convention

Every feature under `src/features/<name>/` MUST contain exactly these 5 folders:

```
features/<name>/
  pages/          # Route-level page components (one per route)
  components/     # Feature-scoped reusable UI components
  services/       # TanStack Query hooks + raw API call functions
  interfaces/     # Feature-scoped types and interfaces
  utils/          # Feature-scoped helper functions
```

## Rules

- **No `ui/` or `api/` folders.** Use `pages/` + `components/` and `services/` respectively.
- **No barrel `index.ts`** files inside features.
- Pages are named `<Name>Page.tsx` (e.g. `DashboardPage.tsx`). They compose components.
- Services are named `<name>Service.ts` (e.g. `dashboardService.ts`). They export TanStack Query hooks (`useXxx`) and raw API functions.
- Interfaces are named `<name>.interfaces.ts`. They hold request/response types, component prop types, and local state types.
- Components stay pure -- no direct API calls. Data comes via props or hooks from `services/`.
- A feature NEVER imports from another feature's internals. Shared code goes to `src/components/`, `src/hooks/`, or `src/types/`.

## Example: Adding a "Projects" feature

```
features/projects/
  pages/ProjectsPage.tsx
  components/ProjectCard.tsx
  components/ProjectFilters.tsx
  services/projectsService.ts    # exports useProjects(), useCreateProject()
  interfaces/projects.interfaces.ts
  utils/formatProjectDate.ts
```

Then add the route in `app/router/routes.tsx` under the DashboardLayout children.
